## Symptom

Outbound remote DMs can be silently deleted. C2c_relay_connector.sync takes with_outbox_lock (c2c_relay_connector.ml:2691) around read+HTTP-send only, then calls write_outbox (the truncating whole-file rewrite) OUTSIDE the lock (~line 2755). Meanwhile append_outbox_entry (1794, the c2c send peer@host enqueue path via c2c_broker.ml:2980 and c2c_mcp_helpers_post_broker.ml:324) never takes the lock at all. Interleaving: sync reads [A] -> seconds of HTTP -> MCP send appends B -> sync write_outbox truncates and rewrites without B -> B lost. Tracked as F2 in .collab/research/2026-04-29-stanza-coder-outbox-relay-state-machine-audit.md (fix never applied); the write-outside-lock placement additionally defeats the lock that does exist.

## Fix direction

Move write_outbox inside the lock window AND wrap append_outbox_entry in with_outbox_lock. Add the interleaving test the 2026-04-29 audit proposed.

## Evidence

Connector review 2026-09-17; verified in source by coordinator (lock at 2691, write after the closing paren, append never locks).